  "final_text": "The September invoice only changes **F2** and the consumption share in **F3**. The payback in F4 stays at 5.0 years, and F1, F5 and F6 aren't affected.\n\n## What the photo shows\nInvoice EL-25-09, billing period 01.09–30.09.2025: **41,200 kWh × 9.50 = 391,400.00 MKD**. The meter readings match the quantity (1,325,550 − 1,284,350 = 41,200 kWh), and the amount matches the quantity times the tariff. The photo is stamped **КОПИЈА** (copy), so for the bank's file it's better to get the original e-invoice from the supplier.\n\n## Two problems in the CSV\n1. **September is missing.** The CSV has no row for EL-25-09. The invoice was issued on 03.10.2025 but seems never to have been booked.\n2. **October is in there twice.** EL-25-10 appears once as the e-invoice (booked 2025-11-05) and again as a scan (booked 2025-12-02). The invoice number, kWh and amount are identical, so it's the same invoice booked twice. Accounting should check whether 367,650 MKD was actually paid twice.\n\nSimply adding up the CSV gives 318.4 MWh. That looks close to the right total, but only because the duplicated October roughly makes up for the missing September.\n\n## Effect on the form\n\n| Field | Before (CSV, Oct counted once, Sep missing) | With the September invoice |\n|---|---|---|\n| **F2** Electricity use 2025 | 279.7 MWh (11 months only) | **320.9 MWh**, full year, based on invoices (≈ 3,048,550 MKD) |\n| **F3** PV yield / share | 180 MWh / 64.4 % | 180 MWh / **≈ 56 %** (*estimate*: the installer's yield, not measured) |\n| **F4** Simple payback | 8,550,000 / (180,000 × 9.50) = **5.0 years** | **5.0 years, unchanged** (*estimate*). The formula doesn't use consumption. |\n\nF2 is no longer an estimate because all 12 months now come from invoices. F3 and F4 must still be marked as estimates because they rely on the installer's 180 MWh figure.\n\n## Not affected\n- **F1, F5, F6** (fines, employees and accidents, certificates): none of the four documents contains this information, so those fields still have to come from the client.\n- **Offer deadline:** the offer is dated 2 September 2026 and valid for 60 days, so it **expires on 1 November 2026**. Neither side has signed it yet.",
